          "collection_date": "2014-10-08",
          "description": {
            "comment": "Puccinia striiformis f. sp. tritici, causing stripe rust of wheat is a serious disease of wheat occurring in most wheat grown areas with cool and moist weather conditions. Puccinia striiformis f. sp. tritici is a macrocyclic, heteroecious fungus that requires living hosts to complete its life cycle. In this project whole genome sequencing of Puccinia striiformis f. sp. tritici Pathotype 38S102 was carried out. This pathotype was first isolated from Neelgiri Hills in 1973 and is avirulent to Yr9.",
